# VolunPeers

Volunteer coordination platform: events, chat, and user management.

## Stack
- Rails 7.1, Ruby 3.3.9, PostgreSQL, Redis (Action Cable)
- Devise (authentication), Pundit (authorization)
- Hotwire (Turbo + Stimulus), Bootstrap 5, Slim templates, Sass
- Cloudinary (image uploads), Geocoder (location search)

## Project conventions
- Authorize every controller action with a Pundit policy; never trust params for access control.
- Views are Slim — keep logic out of templates; use helpers/presenters.
- Real-time chat runs on Action Cable channels backed by Redis.
- Use Stimulus controllers for JS behavior and Turbo Streams for partial updates — avoid ad-hoc jQuery/vanilla JS.
- Location features go through Geocoder scopes, not manual lat/lng math.

<!-- shared:rails-conventions -->
## General Rails conventions
- Prefix all Rails/rake/test commands with `bundle exec`.
- Follow RuboCop; run `bundle exec rubocop -a` before finishing. Match the existing `.rubocop.yml`.
- 2-space indent, no tabs. Thin controllers, RESTful routes; push logic into models, POROs, or service objects.
- Use strong parameters. Never build SQL via string interpolation — use parameter binding / ActiveRecord query methods.
- Rely on Rails auto-escaping in views; avoid `raw`/`html_safe` on user-supplied data.

## Testing
- Framework is **Minitest** (`test/`). Do NOT introduce RSpec.
- Run `bundle exec rails test` (single file: `bundle exec rails test test/models/user_test.rb`); system tests: `bundle exec rails test:system`.
- Add or extend tests for every behavior change; use fixtures in `test/fixtures/`.

## Before finishing
- `bundle exec rubocop -a` clean, `bundle exec rails test` green, and `bundle exec brakeman` for security-sensitive changes.
